    "title": "The Sapiens",
    "desc": "Sapiens: A Brief History of Humankind is a multi-million-copy international bestselling book written by Israeli historian Yuval Noah Harari. Spanning roughly 70,000 years of human history, the narrative seamlessly fuses natural sciences with social sciences to explain how an insignificant ape evolved to dominate planet Earth. Furthermore, he warns that through fast-advancing fields like biotechnology and artificial intelligence, Homo sapiens will likely upgrade or design themselves into entirely different, non-biological entities within a matter of centuries—bringing a definitive end to Sapiens history.",
