    "desc": "Great Expectations by Charles Dickens is a famous 19th-century prose fiction masterpiece that tracks the life, ambition, and moral growth of an orphan named Pip.Pip grows up in rural Kent under the harsh care of his sister and her gentle blacksmith husband, Joe Gargery. His life shifts forever after two encounters: helping an escaped convict named Abel Magwitch, and being hired to visit the bitter, wedding-dress-wearing spinster Miss Havisham and her cruel but beautiful adopted daughter, Estella",
