{
  "model": "store.product",
  "pk": 7,
  "fields": {
    "title": "Hard Times",
    "desc": "Hard Times (originally published in 1854) is Charles Dickens's tenth novel. It stands out as his shortest novel and one of his sharpest pieces of social satire. The book critiques the harsh social and economic conditions of mid-19th-century industrial England.The novel begins with Mr. Thomas Gradgrind sternly lecturing a room full of school children on the importance of facts, and not imagination or emotion, are the key to a good education, and he educates all the children of the school and his own children, Louisa and Tom. When one of his worst students, Sissy Jupe, is abandoned by her father (a circus performer), Mr. Gradgrind takes in Sissy to educate her along with his children according to his sacred system of facts.",
    "price": 450.0,
    "author": "Charles Dickens",
