    "desc": "Rich Dad Poor Dad by Robert T. Kiyosaki and Sharon Lechter was originally published on April 8, 1997. It has gone on to become the number-one personal finance book of all time, selling over 44 million copies worldwide.Rich Dad Poor Dad is a foundational personal finance book framed as a memoir. It details Kiyosaki's upbringing in Hawaii and highlights the starkly different financial mindsets of the two influential father figures in his life.The father of his best friend, who was a high school dropout but a highly street-smart entrepreneur and  He went on to become one of the wealthiest individuals in Hawaii by learning how to build assets and make money work for him.",
