    "desc": "The Bhagavad Gita (meaning \"The Song of God\") is a 700-verse, 18-chapter sacred Hindu scripture written in Epic Sanskrit. It is an integral segment of the ancient Indian epic, the Mahabharata (specifically occupying chapters 23 to 40 of Book VI, the Bhishma Parva). It is a work of sacred philosophical scripture and epic poetry. According to the Hindu spiritual epics, the events took place at the transition between the Dvapara Yuga and Kali Yuga, dating the spoken delivery of the text to approximately 3102 BCE–3067 BCE (making the spoken discourse roughly 5,100 years old)",
